Step 4 Frontend Containerization

This step converted the JerseyHub React and Vite frontend into a production Docker image served by Nginx. It also established the /api reverse-proxy design required for Docker Compose integration.

## Outcome

- Inspected the Vite build configuration and API URL usage.
- Confirmed the Express route prefixes.
- Created a multi-stage frontend Dockerfile.
- Configured Nginx for React Router and API proxying.
- Created frontend/.dockerignore.
- Repaired and verified the npm lock file.
- Built jerseyhub-frontend:1.0.
- Committed and pushed the Step 4 changes.

