## 1 Inspect the frontend

These read-only commands identified the build process, configuration files, and API URL usage.

~~~bash
cd ~/jerseyhub-devops
cat frontend/package.json
find frontend -maxdepth 2 -type f \
  \( -name 'vite.config.*' -o -name '.env.example' -o -name 'Dockerfile' \) -print
grep -R --line-number --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=dist \
  -E 'VITE_API_URL|localhost:2987|axios.create|baseURL' frontend
~~~
The project uses npm run build, which invokes Vite and writes production files to frontend/dist.

## 2 Understand the API URL

~~~javascript
const API_URL =
    import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || "http://localhost:2987";

export default API_URL;
~~~
Components append paths such as /category, /jersey, /cart, /order, and /user. Production uses VITE_API_URL=/api. localhost:2987 cannot be used publicly because it would refer to the visitor's computer.

## 3 Confirm the backend routes

Express mounts routes directly without an /api prefix.

~~~javascript
app.use('/jersey', jerseyRouter);
app.use('/product', productRoute);
app.use('/category', categoryRoute);
app.use('/user', userRouter);
app.use('/cart', cartRoute);
app.use('/order', orderRoute);
app.use('/profile', profileRoute);
~~~
Nginx therefore removes /api before forwarding. /api/category reaches Express as /category.

## 4 Frontend Dockerfile

File: frontend/Dockerfile

~~~dockerfile
FROM node:24-alpine AS build

WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY . .

ARG VITE_API_URL=/api
ENV VITE_API_URL=$VITE_API_URL
ARG VITE_RAZORPAY_ENABLED=false
ENV VITE_RAZORPAY_ENABLED=$VITE_RAZORPAY_ENABLED

RUN npm run build

FROM nginx:alpine
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
COPY --from=build /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
EXPOSE 80
CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]
~~~
The Node stage builds the app. The final stage contains only Nginx, its configuration, and compiled files, so development dependencies are not shipped.

## 5 Nginx configuration

File: frontend/nginx.conf

~~~nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name _;
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index index.html;

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://backend:2987/;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }

    location = /index.html {
        add_header Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate";
        try_files $uri =404;
    }

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    }
}
~~~
The proxy_pass trailing slash removes /api/. try_files supports direct React Router navigation. Docker Compose supplies the hostname backend in Step 5.

