## 7 Repair the lock file

The first npm ci failed because package.json and package-lock.json were out of sync. @emnapi/core and @emnapi/runtime were missing. The lock file was repaired instead of weakening the reproducible build.

~~~bash
docker run --rm \
  --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -e HOME=/tmp \
  -v "$PWD/frontend:/app" -w /app node:24-alpine \
  npm install --package-lock-only
~~~
The corrected graph was verified with the same Node image.

~~~bash
docker run --rm \
  --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -e HOME=/tmp \
  -v "$PWD/frontend:/app" -w /app node:24-alpine npm ci

rm -rf frontend/node_modules
~~~
Verification installed 466 packages and reported zero vulnerabilities.

## 8 Build the image

~~~bash
docker build --progress=plain \
  -t jerseyhub-frontend:1.0 ./frontend

docker image ls jerseyhub-frontend
~~~
The successful build transformed 2,640 modules, generated Vite and PWA output, copied dist into Nginx, and tagged the image.

| Image | Disk usage | Content size |
|---|---:|---:|
| jerseyhub-frontend:1.0 | 96 MB | 26.8 MB |

The chunk-size warning did not fail the build and can be addressed later through code splitting.

